@startuml
title Current authorized retrieval (optimistic revalidation)
actor Caller
participant "Five-tool control plane" as MCP
participant "Endpoint registry" as Registry
participant "Existing access policy" as ACL
participant "Request-local service" as Service
participant "Filesystem / Markdown" as FS
participant "Derived index" as Index
Caller -> MCP : call_endpoint
MCP -> ACL : authenticate / current account and runtime
MCP -> Registry : resolve existing dynamic endpoint / schema
Registry -> Service : authorized bounded arguments
Service -> ACL : root visibility and source-reference boundary
Service -> FS : current root metadata / bounded body
Service -> Index : discover candidate references
note right of Index
  Advisory candidates, not authority.
  Assertion view parses the pinned root directly.
end note
loop admitted candidates only
  Service -> ACL : filter before resolution/aggregation
  Service -> FS : fresh selected metadata and needed bodies
  Service -> Service : preserve revisions, locators and occurrences
end
Service -> FS : refresh reference inventory / membership when applicable
Service -> ACL : current access / edge boundary
Service -> FS : final current revisions
alt drift, ambiguity or revocation observed
  Service --> Caller : discard unavailable context; no hidden details
else current observed inputs
  Service -> Service : compact whole response with pinned read action
  Service --> Caller : packet / explicit partial scope
end
note over Service,FS
  Current inputs != complete topic != verified evidence.
  Metadata/body budgets do not bound inventory or cold-index I/O.
  No NAS-wide atomic snapshot is claimed.
end note
@enduml
